  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Phosphorus trichloride&nbsp;is obtained by the action of thionyl chloride with white phosphorus</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><msub><mi>SOCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><munder><mrow><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>PCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>Phosphorus trichloride is a colourless oily liquid and hydrolyses in the presence of moisture give dibasic phosphorus acid.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><munder><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>HCl</mi></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
